# Ignore by pattern, never by filename — the rule .gitignore learned the hard
# way when data/runs.db arrived four months after data/jobs.db and nobody
# added a second line.

# Never ship anyone's data into an image. The volume carries it instead.
data/
user_profiles/
outputs/
.cache/
*.db

# `tests/` and `baselines/` are NOT excluded, though neither reaches the
# shipping image: they are copied only by the `verify` stage, which
# `--target runtime` stops before. They are code and frozen measurements
# rather than anyone's data, and the exit condition for the container is that
# the suite, the baselines and acceptance all run *inside* it — which the
# exclusion made impossible.

# Secrets. `fly secrets` sets these at runtime; an image with a key baked in
# is a key published to anyone who can pull it.
.env
.env.*
*.pem

# Build inputs that the image rebuilds itself.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Not needed at runtime, and they are most of the context upload.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
docs/
*.md
!README.md
